# Git & GitHub Workflow

Canonical: `CONTRIBUTING.md` · `docs/process/REPOSITORY_GOVERNANCE.md` ·
`docs/process/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md` · `docs/process/CI_REQUIRED_CHECKS.md`

```text
Issue → Branch → Implementation → Commit → Pull Request → Quality CI → Merge
```

## Protect `main`

- **`main` is protected.** Never `git push` commits directly to `main`.
- Always work on a feature/fix branch, open a **pull request**, wait for
  required checks (**Format** | **Analyze** | **Test** | **Validate workflows**),
  then **merge** the PR (`gh pr merge` or GitHub UI).
- Do not force-push or delete `main`.
- Do not commit or merge unless the user explicitly asks (or an approved plan
  requests it). When the user asks to land work: branch → commit → PR → merge.

## Commits

- Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `ci:`, …).
- Stage intentional paths only — never `git add .` / `-A` unless the user
  explicitly asks for a broad commit.

## PRs

- Link Issues (`Closes` / `Refs`) for non-trivial work.
- Fill the PR template; expect Format / Analyze / Test / Validate workflows.
- Do **not** require or reintroduce PR desktop builds (Build macOS / Windows).
- After merge, prefer deleting the head branch.
